B.b9g=s(["You mustn't pay today.","You don't have to pay today.","You should not paying today."],t.s)
B.anM=s(["MUST / HAVE TO = obligation ; DON\u2019T HAVE TO = pas oblig\xe9 (attention : MUSTN\u2019T = interdit !).",'SHOULD / OUGHT TO = conseil bienveillant : "You should practise aloud for 10 minutes."','MIGHT / COULD = possibilit\xe9 mesur\xe9e : "It might rain later, so take an umbrella."'],t.s)
B.boh=new A.ul(["Let's practise modals! Give me one piece of advice using 'should', and one thing you don't have to do this weekend!","You don't have to pay today.","Absence d\u2019obligation = \xab don\u2019t have to \xbb.","You mustn\u2019t come if you are tired (pour dire \xab tu n\u2019es pas oblig\xe9 \xbb). \u274c","Should I prepare slides for tomorrow\u2019s quick catch-up?","Devrais-je pr\xe9parer des diapositives pour le point rapide de demain ?","You don't have to make slides, though a short summary might help everyone stay aligned.","Tu n\u2019es pas oblig\xe9 de faire des diapositives, mais un court r\xe9sum\xe9 pourrait aider tout le monde.","You don't have to come if you're tired. \u2705",B.b9g,"Comment dire \xab Tu n\u2019es pas oblig\xe9 de payer aujourd\u2019hui \xbb ?",B.anM,"Conseiller, exprimer une obligation ou une probabilit\xe9","Modaux de nuance : Must, Have to, Should, Might","\xab Mustn\u2019t \xbb signifie \xab il est interdit de \xbb, jamais \xab tu n\u2019es pas oblig\xe9 \xbb."])
B.b7w=s(["to listen","listening to","listen"],t.s)
B.b7c=s(['Verbes suivis de -ING : enjoy, finish, avoid, suggest, keep, mind, look forward to ("I enjoy speaking English").','Verbes suivis de TO + base : decide, want, hope, plan, promise, manage ("I decided to study daily").',"Pi\xe8ge c\xe9l\xe8bre : apr\xe8s \xab look forward to \xbb et \xab be used to \xbb, \xab to \xbb est une pr\xe9position \u2192 toujours -ING !"],t.s)
B.boi=new A.ul(["Tell me one thing you really enjoy doing every week, and one thing you're looking forward to doing soon!","listening to","\xab Enjoy \xbb est toujours suivi de la forme en -ING (+ \xab to \xbb avec listen).","I look forward to hear from you. \u274c","Are you looking forward to presenting your project next week?","As-tu h\xe2te de pr\xe9senter ton projet la semaine prochaine ?","Yes! I finished preparing my notes and I'm trying to avoid speaking too fast.","Oui ! J\u2019ai fini de pr\xe9parer mes notes et j\u2019essaie d\u2019\xe9viter de parler trop vite.","I look forward to hearing from you. \u2705",B.b7w,'Compl\xe9tez : "I really enjoy _____ English podcasts while walking."',B.b7c,"Enjoy doing, Decide to do, Look forward to + -ing","G\xe9rondif (-ing) vs Infinitif (to + verbe)","\xab Look forward to \xbb est toujours suivi d\u2019un nom ou d\u2019un verbe en -ING."])
B.b8u=s(["isn't she","doesn't she","no"],t.s)
B.bay=s(['Phrase affirmative \u2192 tag n\xe9gatif : "You live in Dakar, don\u2019t you?" / "She\u2019s brilliant, isn\u2019t she?".','Phrase n\xe9gative \u2192 tag affirmatif : "You haven\u2019t seen this yet, have you?".',"Les question tags rendent votre anglais imm\xe9diatement plus chaleureux et conversationnel."],t.s)
B.bol=new A.ul(["Let's make our chat super natural! Say something about your week or weather using a question tag like 'isn't it?' or 'don't you?'","doesn't she","\xab Speaks \xbb au pr\xe9sent simple \u2192 auxiliaire \xab doesn\u2019t she? \xbb.","This coffee is very good, no? \u274c","It's a lovely morning today, isn't it?","C\u2019est une belle matin\xe9e aujourd\u2019hui, n\u2019est-ce pas ?","It really is! You've been practising every day this week, haven't you?","Vraiment ! Tu as pratiqu\xe9 chaque jour cette semaine, pas vrai ?","This coffee is really good, isn't it? \u2705",B.b8u,'Compl\xe9tez : "She speaks English very clearly, _____?"',B.bay,"\xab It\u2019s great, isn\u2019t it? \xbb, \xab You work here, don\u2019t you? \xbb","Questions naturelles & Question Tags","En anglais naturel, on ne termine pas par \xab , no? \xbb : on reprend l\u2019auxiliaire."])
B.bga=s(["By the way","However","Therefore"],t.s)
B.b8H=s(["\xab To be honest / Honestly \xbb : introduire une opinion sinc\xe8re sans brusquer.","\xab By the way \xbb : changer de sujet en douceur dans une discussion.","\xab Actually / In fact \xbb : pr\xe9ciser ou nuancer gentiment une information."],t.s)
B.boj=new A.ul(["Tell me something honest about learning English using 'To be honest' or 'Actually', then switch topics with 'By the way'!","By the way","\xab By the way \xbb = au fait / \xe0 propos.","I will tell you the truth, I prefer reading. \u274c","By the way, did you get a chance to try the new learning routine?","Au fait, as-tu eu l\u2019occasion d\u2019essayer la nouvelle routine d\u2019apprentissage ?","To be honest, I was skeptical at first \u2014 in fact, it ended up saving me an hour a day!","Pour \xeatre honn\xeate, j\u2019\xe9tais sceptique au d\xe9but \u2014 en fait, \xe7a a fini par me faire gagner une heure par jour !","To be honest, I actually prefer reading over watching videos. \u2705",B.bga,"Quel marqueur sert \xe0 changer gentiment de sujet (\xab Au fait... \xbb) ?",B.b8H,"By the way, Actually, Basically, To be honest, In fact","Relier ses id\xe9es comme un natif (Discourse Markers)","Ces petits marqueurs donnent instantan\xe9ment du naturel et du rythme \xe0 l\u2019oral."])
B.b8L=s(["This approach is more clearer.","This approach is much clearer.","This approach is very clearer."],t.s)
B.bg0=s(["Adjectif court (1 syllabe) : -er / the -est (faster, clearer, the best). Adjectif long : more / the most (more efficient).",'Renforcer un comparatif : \xab much / far / a lot \xbb devant le comparatif ("much easier", jamais "more easier").','\xc9galit\xe9 / contraste doux : "Speaking isn\u2019t as intimidating as I thought."'],t.s)
B.bog=new A.ul(["Compare two skills, tools, or habits in your life using 'much better', 'far more useful', or 'as ... as'!","This approach is much clearer.","Pour intensifier un comparatif, utilisez \xab much / far / a lot \xbb.","This method is more better and more easy. \u274c","Do you find listening easier than speaking?","Trouves-tu l\u2019\xe9coute plus facile que l\u2019expression orale ?","Listening is much easier, though speaking is becoming far more natural every week.","L\u2019\xe9coute est beaucoup plus facile, mais parler devient bien plus naturel chaque semaine.","This method is much better and far easier. \u2705",B.b8L,"Choisissez la phrase 100 % naturelle :",B.bg0,"Much faster, far more practical, not nearly as hard as","Comparer & nuancer : Comparatifs, Superlatifs & As...As","On utilise \xab much / far \xbb (jamais \xab more \xbb) devant un comparatif irr\xe9gulier ou en -er."])
B.bev=s(["was","is been","were"],t.s)
B.b9L=s(['Voix passive = BE (au bon temps) + participe pass\xe9 (V3) : "The report was sent", "The system is being upgraded".','Tr\xe8s utile quand l\u2019action compte plus que l\u2019auteur : "All measurements were verified before publication."','Structure pratique : "needs to be + V3" ("This bug needs to be fixed today").'],t.s)
B.bok=new A.ul(["Describe a project or task you worked on recently using at least one passive sentence like 'was built', 'was solved', or 'needs to be improved'!","was","Sujet singulier au pass\xe9 (\xab last week \xbb) \u2192 \xab was tested \xbb.","The document was send yesterday. \u274c","Has the new schedule been shared with everyone yet?","Le nouveau planning a-t-il d\xe9j\xe0 \xe9t\xe9 partag\xe9 avec tout le monde ?","Yes, it was sent this morning, and a reminder will be posted tonight.","Oui, il a \xe9t\xe9 envoy\xe9 ce matin, et un rappel sera publi\xe9 ce soir.","The document was sent yesterday. \u2705",B.bev,'Compl\xe9tez : "The new prototype _____ tested thoroughly last week."',B.b9L,"Is being updated, Was delivered, Needs to be verified","Voix passive & style clair en contexte pro","La voix passive utilise toujours la 3e colonne (participe pass\xe9 : send \u2192 sent)."])
B.b7I=s([B.boh,B.boi,B.bol,B.boj,B.bog,B.bok],A.H("w<+amyPrompt,ans,ansExp,avoid,d1En,d1Fr,d2En,d2Fr,natural,opts,q,rules,subtitleFr,topicFr,trapExplain(d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,U<d>,d,U<d>,d,d,d)>"))
